epos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible since 4.4.dev3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 22631) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7216) - AMD Ryzen 7 7840HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nI've created an Android Plugin that utilizes ExoPlayer and the new obtainable Android Surface to display a Video on it.\nThe Video though is flipped horizontally and vertically.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/936ca41a-5f41-4b69-8352-1687df6bea24)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nWhen cloning / downloading the Repo there is a demo at plugin/demo/scenes/main.\n\nBut for a basic implementation you would need to:\n- Create a Java/Kotlin Code that has a Surface as Input\n- Instantiate a new ExoPlayer and attach the Surface to it\n- load a video\n\n\n\n```kotlin\nfun createExoPlayerSurface(surface: Surface, videoUri : String){\nrunOnUiThread{\n   val newExoPlayer = activity?.let{ctx -> ExoPlayer.Builder(ctx).build()\n   newExoPlayer.setVideoSurface(surface)\n   val mediaItem = MediaItem.fromUri(videoUri)\n   newExoPlayer.setMediaItem(mediaItem)\n   newExoPlayer.prepare()\n   newExoPlayer.play()\n\n   }\n}\n```\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nThis is the direct link to my \"Addons Repo\" \nhttps://github.com/bnjmntmm/godot-exoplayer\n","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.git